message: "If you use this software or the audit protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "structured-data-fm-reliability-research: split-conditioned selective-prediction reliability audit for tabular models"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-02"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21130297"
authors:
  - family-names: "Fu"
    given-names: "Zeyu"
    email: "fuzeyu09@gmail.com"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reliability-evaluation protocol and benchmark audit showing that random-split
  validation overstates tabular-model reliability: on 14 keyed OpenML datasets,
  leave-group-out / rolling-origin splits collapse risk-coverage (AURC) and
  split-conformal coverage; uncertainty-ranked abstention repairs most of it
  (13/14 datasets, Holm-robust) across XGBoost, LightGBM, and the TabICLv2
  tabular foundation model, and a Mondrian group-conditional conformal add-on
  is a pre-registered null. Code only; datasets are fetched on demand and carry
  their own licenses (see DATA_MANIFEST.md).
keywords:
  - tabular machine learning
  - selective prediction
  - conformal prediction
  - distribution shift
  - reliability evaluation
  - foundation models
